(801422, 88837, 3649, '<td valign="top">straight out of a brochure. you caught some great light and settings coming together here. the bike and woman sitting stand out nicely since the background haze and grass are both dull in color. the line of the wood in the bottom left reflects the angle of the bike nicely as well. Great ad-based shot.</td>', 'straight out of a brochure. you caught some great light and settings coming together here. the bike and woman sitting stand out nicely since the background haze and grass are both dull in color. the line of the wood in the bottom left reflects the angle of the bike nicely as well. Great ad-based shot.', '2004-07-07 23:55:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(801434, 89013, 327, '<td valign="top">Your idea was good but your lighting was just too strong. Try using a plastic bag or tissue paper over your flash. Good luck.</td>', 'Your idea was good but your lighting was just too strong. Try using a plastic bag or tissue paper over your flash. Good luck.', '2004-07-08 00:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(801437, 87333, 20957, '<td valign="top">I love stella, but i think the lighting is way too harsh. I think the bottle is awesome and the glass detracts from it too much.  i really like the texture the condensation gives the bottom most part of the bottel, just too harsh a light.. Maybe  a scrim next time.</td>', 'I love stella, but i think the lighting is way too harsh. I think the bottle is awesome and the glass detracts from it too much.  i really like the texture the condensation gives the bottom most part of the bottel, just too harsh a light.. Maybe  a scrim next time.', '2004-07-08 00:03:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(801440, 89224, 327, '<td valign="top">Looks washed out from the sunlight. Not any color depth. Maybe a UV filter might help. Good luck.</td>', 'Looks washed out from the sunlight. Not any color depth. Maybe a UV filter might help. Good luck.', '2004-07-08 00:03:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(801445, 86774, 327, '<td valign="top">Dark would be the right word. There is always a reflection problem with shooting this type of foil paper. To control it try lighting from the rear or bouncing the light off a nearby wall.</td>', 'Dark would be the right word. There is always a reflection problem with shooting this type of foil paper. To control it try lighting from the rear or bouncing the light off a nearby wall.', '2004-07-08 00:04:34.000000', NULL, 1),
