(810563, 89101, 22011, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments..  <br/> <br/>Another lesson learnt about DPC.  Check/correct the whitebalance before uploading a pic to DPC ;-).<br/> <br/>I''m quite happy with how it placed though, I don''t have high expectations of a photo that took me all of 5 minutes from idea to upload.</td>', 'Thanks for your comments..   Another lesson learnt about DPC.  Check/correct the whitebalance before uploading a pic to DPC ;-). I''m quite happy with how it placed though, I don''t have high expectations of a photo that took me all of 5 minutes from idea to upload.', '2004-07-14 06:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(810600, 89275, 11738, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hgpayne:</b></div><hr/><i> I gotta ask -- where you inspired at all by my shot like this in an earlier challenge?<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=30993" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/121/thumb/30993.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/121/thumb/30993.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/121/thumb/30993.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nope.  Hadn''t even seen it.<br/> <br/>And to those who scored this below 4, I know this isn''t the greatest shot, but I think I like the slugs better than I like you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.hawkins.nu/gtchat/images/yes.gif'', strrpos(''//www.hawkins.nu/gtchat/images/yes.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.hawkins.nu/gtchat/images/yes.gif"/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-14 07:05:07.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by hgpayne: I gotta ask -- where you inspired at all by my shot like this in an earlier challenge?   Nope.  Hadn''t even seen it. And to those who scored this below 4, I know this isn''t the greatest shot, but I think I like the slugs better than I like you ', '2004-07-14 07:52:55.000000', '2004-07-14 08:05:07.000000', 0),
(810607, 88132, 19333, '<td valign="top">Nice pic, good use of the rule of thirds. I do agree with Idalleck on the watch''s face sharpness issue.<br/>Just being picky, Rolex ads always have the time set at 10 to 10 :)</td>', 'Nice pic, good use of the rule of thirds. I do agree with Idalleck on the watch''s face sharpness issue.Just being picky, Rolex ads always have the time set at 10 to 10 :)', '2004-07-14 08:02:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(810638, 88933, 1570, '<td valign="top">thanks a lot for all your great comments, i had lots of fun with this picture! and for those who said that they''d choose another model, that''s fine, my husband probably wouldn''t choose to pose for you either...</td>', 'thanks a lot for all your great comments, i had lots of fun with this picture! and for those who said that they''d choose another model, that''s fine, my husband probably wouldn''t choose to pose for you either...', '2004-07-14 08:53:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(810689, 89251, 6202, '<td valign="top">From the beginning I questioned my choice in titles for this photo.  I wished I had went with my other thoughts and called this something to the effect of Junior Acheivement or Enterprising Youth.  I wasn''t trying to sell the idea of Smuckers but rather the idea of a child wanting to work to make money.  <br/> <br/>The pitcher with Smuckers on it was used cause it was available and I just didn''t have time to go to the store for a plain glass pitcher so I worked with what I had.<br/> <br/>As for the comments about his expression....well as I took the photo he was standing there yelling...Lemonade 25 cents...one quarter, two dimes and a nickel, five nickels, or 25 pennies...Oh what a street barker I have on my hands....LOL<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the beginning I questioned my choice in titles for this photo.  I wished I had went with my other thoughts and called this something to the effect of Junior Acheivement or Enterprising Youth.  I wasn''t trying to sell the idea of Smuckers but rather the idea of a child wanting to work to make money.   The pitcher with Smuckers on it was used cause it was available and I just didn''t have time to go to the store for a plain glass pitcher so I worked with what I had. As for the comments about his expression....well as I took the photo he was standing there yelling...Lemonade 25 cents...one quarter, two dimes and a nickel, five nickels, or 25 pennies...Oh what a street barker I have on my hands....LOL ', '2004-07-14 09:28:51.000000', NULL, 0),
