(818116, 87816, 22922, '<td valign="top">Aloha from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is definitely a tough subject to capture.  Keyboards are difficult to light properly, and DOF is tricky as well.  It looks like you have the right idea with the angle of the shot, just deepen the DOF to bring more of the image into focus.  A little more ambient light would make this image sharper, since it is very dark right now.  <br/> <br/>I think as far as meeting the challenge, this image needs a little bit more relevance.  Keep in mind that the image should suggest or identify your specific product, and at the moment this could be any computer.  It would also help if you cleaned the touch-mouse since it looks very dirty in the image, and not appealling as a product feature.<br/> <br/>Your composition is well thought out, and you have a strong image here with a few tweaks, but this is more of a nice stock photo rather than a branded advertisement.</td>', 'Aloha from the Critique Club! This is definitely a tough subject to capture.  Keyboards are difficult to light properly, and DOF is tricky as well.  It looks like you have the right idea with the angle of the shot, just deepen the DOF to bring more of the image into focus.  A little more ambient light would make this image sharper, since it is very dark right now.   I think as far as meeting the challenge, this image needs a little bit more relevance.  Keep in mind that the image should suggest or identify your specific product, and at the moment this could be any computer.  It would also help if you cleaned the touch-mouse since it looks very dirty in the image, and not appealling as a product feature. Your composition is well thought out, and you have a strong image here with a few tweaks, but this is more of a nice stock photo rather than a branded advertisement.', '2004-07-20 12:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(818126, 89306, 22922, '<td valign="top">Aloha from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>You clearly have a strong image and idea here.  The B&amp;W flatters the glass subjects, and the soft light lends a late-night club aura to the image.  <br/> <br/>I''m a little distracted by the dusty table and the blurred line in the left forground.  Maybe a tighter crop would get that distracting line out, although you''d lose the bottom of the martini glass. I would also use a smaller ISO (100 or even 50) to get rid of all the noise.<br/> <br/>Challenge-wise, you really should have the whole logo readable, or at least a sharper focus on the "Bacardi Bat" if you want that to identify your ad.  Having an actual drink prepared would also add to the image, perhaps with a curl of citrus to contrast the stark setup? If you don''t actually have full bottles, it''s worth it to substitute some other liquid so they don''t look empty.  The empty bottles with the empty glass seem kind of bland, when you are trying to evoke excitement. <br/> <br/>Your focus is quite good, and your DOF looks correct.  The shot angle is nice, it makes the eye want to look a bit longer at the image.  from your comment, I''m guessing this was your first entry, and you didn''t realize the text wouldn''t show up with the image.  It happens to everyone, and your ad stood up quite well on its own.</td>', 'Aloha from the Critique Club! You clearly have a strong image and idea here.  The B&W flatters the glass subjects, and the soft light lends a late-night club aura to the image.   I''m a little distracted by the dusty table and the blurred line in the left forground.  Maybe a tighter crop would get that distracting line out, although you''d lose the bottom of the martini glass. I would also use a smaller ISO (100 or even 50) to get rid of all the noise. Challenge-wise, you really should have the whole logo readable, or at least a sharper focus on the "Bacardi Bat" if you want that to identify your ad.  Having an actual drink prepared would also add to the image, perhaps with a curl of citrus to contrast the stark setup? If you don''t actually have full bottles, it''s worth it to substitute some other liquid so they don''t look empty.  The empty bottles with the empty glass seem kind of bland, when you are trying to evoke excitement.  Your focus is quite good, and your DOF looks correct.  The shot angle is nice, it makes the eye want to look a bit longer at the image.  from your comment, I''m guessing this was your first entry, and you didn''t realize the text wouldn''t show up with the image.  It happens to everyone, and your ad stood up quite well on its own.', '2004-07-20 12:47:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(818129, 89102, 825, '<td valign="top">nice beer shot. my suggestions would be to back off the USM. logo looks like it was added on - different sharpening, less foam detail. the glass has some dark spots that distract, looks like dirt. may be foam shadows that were over sharpened. you''re on the edge for contrast - good control! saturation is good, it would be fun to print as a large - wall size image! thanks for sharing!</td>', 'nice beer shot. my suggestions would be to back off the USM. logo looks like it was added on - different sharpening, less foam detail. the glass has some dark spots that distract, looks like dirt. may be foam shadows that were over sharpened. you''re on the edge for contrast - good control! saturation is good, it would be fun to print as a large - wall size image! thanks for sharing!', '2004-07-20 12:50:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(818211, 89102, 22912, '<td valign="top">Wow! What a nice surprise! I just got back home, after being out of country (and with no chance to check to see how my pic was doing). Thank you all for the comments that I have gotten, both on this picture and my first entry (the "Extraordinary" challenge). As I am fairly new to the world of digital photography and the digital darkroom, I appreciate all the input you give me!<br/> <br/>Once more; Thanx!<br/> <br/>Audun</td>', 'Wow! What a nice surprise! I just got back home, after being out of country (and with no chance to check to see how my pic was doing). Thank you all for the comments that I have gotten, both on this picture and my first entry (the "Extraordinary" challenge). As I am fairly new to the world of digital photography and the digital darkroom, I appreciate all the input you give me! Once more; Thanx! Audun', '2004-07-20 14:02:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(818387, 88184, 16529, '<td valign="top">In this photo, the background takes away from the photo a lot! The highlight from the light source in the upper left also slightly takes away from the photo! Great subject matter though, good thinking!</td>', 'In this photo, the background takes away from the photo a lot! The highlight from the light source in the upper left also slightly takes away from the photo! Great subject matter though, good thinking!', '2004-07-20 17:22:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(818390, 89243, 16529, '<td valign="top">I like the idea behind this photo! I like the fork where it is...I think that it gives the onlooker the apeal that YOU are eating the brownie mix out of the package! Around the edges, the photo seems to be blurred. The photo could be more clear and concise!</td>', 'I like the idea behind this photo! I like the fork where it is...I think that it gives the onlooker the apeal that YOU are eating the brownie mix out of the package! Around the edges, the photo seems to be blurred. The photo could be more clear and concise!', '2004-07-20 17:25:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(818392, 88364, 16529, '<td valign="top">I like the photo...sneaky way to advertise your business! The background towards the right side could be covered by more buttons.</td>', 'I like the photo...sneaky way to advertise your business! The background towards the right side could be covered by more buttons.', '2004-07-20 17:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(818721, 89290, 22734, '<td valign="top">From the critique club:<br/>  Yes, neon and night are very magical. It is very difficult to take a bad shot of neon lights provided the exposure is all right.<br/>  Now, since this is an advertising challenge I would have looked more closely at the subject. The sign has a lot of lights blown out and of course, the lamp does not help. Advertising shots are very demmanding because a very big budget is devoted to this art and thr great part of the cost is on the preparation. <br/>  I believe you made this challenge all the more difficult because you selected this subject.<br/>  Yet, if you discount the spirit of the challenge, there is a lot to be said about this shot. It is like the photographer simply wanted to bring the name detached from its physical body. A nice composition because the viewer is asked to search. Such pictures bear great strength when the viewer is rewarded with an additional detail that was immediately hidden.<br/>  This is exactly what my eyes do. They search and all I can do is surmize the structure. Again, take heart, it is a good picture, but not one to advertise the establishment. It is rather more a recording, but a well composed one.<br/>  This is certainly one approach to composition and I will make no suggestions to improve cropping because the empty night help create the pleasing blue neon.<br/>  My advise is to consider the challenge and select the simplest denominator of something you can control. You will be surprised at the results.</td>', 'From the critique club:  Yes, neon and night are very magical. It is very difficult to take a bad shot of neon lights provided the exposure is all right.  Now, since this is an advertising challenge I would have looked more closely at the subject. The sign has a lot of lights blown out and of course, the lamp does not help. Advertising shots are very demmanding because a very big budget is devoted to this art and thr great part of the cost is on the preparation.   I believe you made this challenge all the more difficult because you selected this subject.  Yet, if you discount the spirit of the challenge, there is a lot to be said about this shot. It is like the photographer simply wanted to bring the name detached from its physical body. A nice composition because the viewer is asked to search. Such pictures bear great strength when the viewer is rewarded with an additional detail that was immediately hidden.  This is exactly what my eyes do. They search and all I can do is surmize the structure. Again, take heart, it is a good picture, but not one to advertise the establishment. It is rather more a recording, but a well composed one.  This is certainly one approach to composition and I will make no suggestions to improve cropping because the empty night help create the pleasing blue neon.  My advise is to consider the challenge and select the simplest denominator of something you can control. You will be surprised at the results.', '2004-07-20 22:21:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(836895, 89287, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Kavey Critique</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Viewpoint is unusual but overall image seems very tilted.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>As above, the tilt does make this look less professional and could have been corrected with a small rotation of the image followed by a crop. The colours are vivid which is appealing and the water droplets do add interest but there isn''t really a focal point for me - where should my eye end up? <br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>I like that it''s not completely flat yet doesn''t distract from the subject.<br/> <br/><b>Technical</b> <br/>Lighting seems harsh - perhaps diffusing the light source with a white cloth or tissue might help. <br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Yes, though it seems more a case of showing me the product than really selling it''s qualities.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>An acceptable image but one that could be improved a great deal by a few simple changes to lighting and rotation. That said, content does lack "punch".<br/></td>', 'Kavey Critique  Initial thoughts Viewpoint is unusual but overall image seems very tilted. Composition/ Content As above, the tilt does make this look less professional and could have been corrected with a small rotation of the image followed by a crop. The colours are vivid which is appealing and the water droplets do add interest but there isn''t really a focal point for me - where should my eye end up?  Background I like that it''s not completely flat yet doesn''t distract from the subject. Technical Lighting seems harsh - perhaps diffusing the light source with a white cloth or tissue might help.  Fits The Challenge Yes, though it seems more a case of showing me the product than really selling it''s qualities. My Opinion On The Photo An acceptable image but one that could be improved a great deal by a few simple changes to lighting and rotation. That said, content does lack "punch".', '2004-08-02 10:19:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(861132, 88657, 2780, '<td valign="top">The final shot, in my opinion, looks too much like a snapshot and not an advertisement at all. I don''t think desaturating the background would have helped, but getting rid of it completely would have. Doing the same shot with a white background would look much more like a pro advert. The focus is meant to be on the glasses, but the background is just too distracting here. Also, the focus seems slightly off. Either that, or you used the wrong settings when sharpening in post-processing. The lighting is a bit harsh on her neck and hair too. To get the glasses looking more appealing for the advert, they should have some kind of catchlight in them to make them look shiney and new, and add character.</td>', 'The final shot, in my opinion, looks too much like a snapshot and not an advertisement at all. I don''t think desaturating the background would have helped, but getting rid of it completely would have. Doing the same shot with a white background would look much more like a pro advert. The focus is meant to be on the glasses, but the background is just too distracting here. Also, the focus seems slightly off. Either that, or you used the wrong settings when sharpening in post-processing. The lighting is a bit harsh on her neck and hair too. To get the glasses looking more appealing for the advert, they should have some kind of catchlight in them to make them look shiney and new, and add character.', '2004-08-16 05:49:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(862088, 88326, 25233, '<td valign="top">More newspaper in veiw would be better i think.</td>', 'More newspaper in veiw would be better i think.', '2004-08-16 18:32:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(882051, 89274, 11832, '<td valign="top">well, im probably stating what everyone else has here, but a full bottle, or even half empty  bottle would look better. Also, maybe if the flame was the main source of light, with just a separte light on the jose cuervo would be better.</td>', 'well, im probably stating what everyone else has here, but a full bottle, or even half empty  bottle would look better. Also, maybe if the flame was the main source of light, with just a separte light on the jose cuervo would be better.', '2004-08-29 00:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
